/-!
# A245284

For any composite number n with more than a single prime factor, take the polynomial defined by the product of the terms (x-pi)^ei, where pi are the prime factors of n with multiplicities ei. Integrate this polynomial from the minimum to the maximum value of pi. This sequence lists the numbers for which the integral is an integer.

The 53 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

